{"task":{"id":"ready_valid_slot","spec":"A single registered 8-bit ready/valid slot without empty-slot combinational bypass. out_valid indicates occupied state; out_data is the stored byte, unspecified when invalid. in_ready = !occupied || out_ready. A rising edge accepts input when in_valid && in_ready and consumes output when out_valid && out_ready; simultaneous consume/accept replaces the byte without a bubble. With output stalled, valid data remains stable. Reset empties the slot and clears stored data.
Use one SystemVerilog module with the exact interface. All state updates on rising clk. rst is synchronous, active high, and has priority. No other modules, file I/O, delays, or simulation-only behavior in the DUT.","interface":{"top":"ready_valid_slot","ports":[{"name":"clk","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"rst","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"in_valid","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"in_data","direction":"input","width":8,"signed":false},{"name":"in_ready","direction":"output","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"out_valid","direction":"output","width":1,"signed":false},{"name":"out_data","direction":"output","width":8,"signed":false},{"name":"out_ready","direction":"input","width":1,"signed":false}]},"constraints":"SystemVerilog; xczu3eg-sbva484-1-e; post-synthesis clock clk at 5 ns; simulation seed 1."},"current":{"revision_id":"49474394-897c-4052-bac2-7c35b81a524e","source_sha256":"3da1be109980ff531ae5c1b2eeed4d0ebe717560b7f8db1cb5cf7beaadda6153","source":"module ready_valid_slot(
  input  logic       clk,
  input  logic       rst,
  input  logic       in_valid,
  input  logic [7:0] in_data,
  output logic       in_ready,
  output logic       out_valid,
  output logic [7:0] out_data,
  input  logic       out_ready
);

  logic       occupied;
  logic [7:0] stored;
  logic       accept;
  logic       consume;

  assign in_ready  = ~occupied | out_ready;
  assign out_valid = occupied;
  assign out_data  = stored;

  assign accept  = in_valid & in_ready;
  assign consume = occupied & out_ready;

  always_ff @(posedge clk) begin
    if (rst) begin
      occupied <= 1'b0;
      stored   <= 8'h00;
    end else begin
      if (accept) begin
        stored   <= in_data;
        occupied <= 1'b1;
      end else if (consume) begin
        occupied <= 1'b0;
      end
    end
  end

endmodule
"},"verification_key":null,"observed":null,"verification_state":"UNVERIFIED","history":[],"guidance":[],"additional_diagnostics":[],"omitted":[]}

